cience and Medicine in Sport</source><year>2004</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>38</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15214599</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1440-2440(04)80275-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fiatarone</surname><given-names>MA</given-names><suffix>O Neill, EF, Ryan, ND, Clements, KM, Solares, GP, Nelson, ME, Roberts, SB, Kehayias, JJ, Kipsitz, LA, Evans, WJ.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Exercise training and nutritional supplementation for physical frailty in very elderly people</article-title><source>The New England Journal of Medicine</source><year>1994</year><volume>330</volume><fpage>1769</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8190152</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJM199406233302501</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ashenden</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Silagy</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Weller</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A systematic review of the effectiveness of promoting lifestyle change in general practice</article-title><source>Family Practice</source><year>1997</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>160</fpage><lpage>176</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9137956</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/fampra/14.2.160</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B37"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sims</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Duffy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilton</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The vagaries of self reports of physical activity behaviour: a problem revisited and a